# .htaccess is ignored by default (line above), but these two are access
# control, not local machine config. If they are not in git then a server set up
# with "git clone" or "git pull" silently runs without them:
#   system/.htaccess   - blocks direct web access to system/*.php
#   pages/.htaccess    - CORS headers the page builder relies on
#
# There is deliberately no install/.htaccess. It was removed after <Files> and
# <IfFile> were both measured to be misapplied by LiteSpeed: the rules denied
# the installer's own stylesheet, logo and every step after the first, making
# the wizard unusable. The installer is instead locked by install/guard.php,
# which is plain PHP and cannot be misparsed or disabled by server config.
# !system/.htaccess
# pages/ is a generated directory and stays ignored, but the CORS rules have to
# be in git. Un-ignoring the directory itself is required first: git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so a bare "!pages/.htaccess" is ignored.
!pages/
pages/*
!pages/.htaccess

